  I've figured out the spellbook price - to - spell level ratio: You
read a book that has been appraised, if you can memorise the runes,
you then look at the spell you learnt in the spell screen ("Z"). After
a few, you'll notice that each spell level is equivilant to 50
zorkminds - as a 'sell' price. It's double that for a 'buy' price.
Only thing that is sometimes funny, is when you get a book priced at
something like 113 zorkminds (like the red one I have here). Then you
have to take a chance at it being a 2nd or 3rd level one. When playing
safe, always assume it's the highest. The higher the spell level, the
tougher it is to read. Play a few Wizards and carefully test all this.
It really helps, trust me.

